##
    Documentation that has come apart from what it documents.

    None of this stops a build on its own. The single error at the bottom is what rejects the
    file — it is here because a sample under 'compile' has to be rejected, and a stale doc is
    never reason enough.
##

global model Program

    ##
        @summary: Adds up to a limit.
        @limit: what to count to.
        @yields: the total.
        @summary: and the summary again, which the first one already carried.
    ##
    global integer function Total(integer n)
        integer sum = 0;

        for i = 1 to n
            sum = sum + i;
        end for

        yield sum;
    end function

    ##
        @summary: Writes a line and gives nothing back.
        @yields: a value that does not exist.
    ##
    global function Announce(string text)
        Console.WriteLine(text);
    end function

    function Main()
        ##
            @summary: a statement cannot be documented, so this reaches nothing.
        ##
        Console.WriteLine(Program.Total(4));

        integer wrong = "not a number";
        Console.WriteLine(wrong);
    end function

end model
